WEBVTT

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.280
You've been using agents for years.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.580
You just didn't know it.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.320
The filter that moves a newsletter out

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.240
of your inbox.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.340
The phone that says traffic is heavy,

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.220
leave now.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.620
The playlist that somehow knows your taste.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.410
Each one watches something,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.570
decides something,

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.490
and acts.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.381
The agents in this guide are the

00:00:22.381 --> 00:00:23.201
same idea,

00:00:23.201 --> 00:00:24.221
only much bigger.

00:00:24.221 --> 00:00:25.941
They don't do one clever thing.

00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:27.531
They do many things in a row,

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:28.791
adapting as they go.

00:00:29.491 --> 00:00:31.381
Every agent runs the same loop.

00:00:31.451 --> 00:00:32.191
Observe:

00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:33.561
take in what's there.

00:00:33.671 --> 00:00:34.271
Plan:

00:00:34.271 --> 00:00:35.601
decide what to do.

00:00:35.771 --> 00:00:36.311
Act:

00:00:36.311 --> 00:00:37.151
do it.

00:00:37.151 --> 00:00:37.671
Check:

00:00:37.671 --> 00:00:38.591
did it work?

00:00:38.591 --> 00:00:39.621
If not,

00:00:39.711 --> 00:00:40.971
round it goes again,

00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:42.521
with what it just learned.

00:00:42.551 --> 00:00:44.911
A simple agent goes round once.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.091
A powerful one goes round dozens of

00:00:47.091 --> 00:00:47.941
times.

00:00:48.507 --> 00:00:50.147
What an agent can do depends on

00:00:50.147 --> 00:00:50.987
its tools.

00:00:50.987 --> 00:00:52.887
Picture a smart new employee at an

00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:53.737
empty desk.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:54.407
Clever,

00:00:54.407 --> 00:00:55.357
but stuck.

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:56.707
Give them a login,

00:00:56.707 --> 00:00:58.187
and they can track the work.

00:00:58.187 --> 00:00:59.547
A key to the project,

00:00:59.547 --> 00:01:00.607
and they can change it.

00:01:00.607 --> 00:01:01.607
A key to launch,

00:01:01.607 --> 00:01:02.767
and they can ship it.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.397
The tools are the access,

00:01:04.407 --> 00:01:06.387
and you decide which keys to hand

00:01:06.387 --> 00:01:07.237
over.

00:01:07.615 --> 00:01:09.295
An agent is not a person.

00:01:09.295 --> 00:01:11.665
It has no goals and no feelings.

00:01:11.735 --> 00:01:13.915
It predicts the most useful next step

00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:15.015
from what it can see.

00:01:15.015 --> 00:01:16.935
So you don't need to motivate it.

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:18.155
You need to be clear.

00:01:18.155 --> 00:01:20.225
And it will be confidently wrong.

00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:22.255
It will solve the wrong problem with

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:23.235
beautiful precision,

00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:24.515
and keep going,

00:01:24.515 --> 00:01:25.375
tirelessly,

00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:26.665
in the wrong direction.

00:01:27.655 --> 00:01:29.085
Agents come in a spectrum,

00:01:29.095 --> 00:01:31.225
autocomplete guesses your next word,

00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:33.225
chat assistants answer your questions.

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.295
Tool -equipped agents have hands,

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.255
they read files and run commands.

00:01:37.255 --> 00:01:39.295
And autonomous agents work on their own

00:01:39.295 --> 00:01:40.405
for long stretches.

00:01:40.535 --> 00:01:42.835
You can close your laptop and come

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.055
back to finished work,

00:01:44.055 --> 00:01:45.345
waiting for your review.

00:01:46.116 --> 00:01:47.246
One more idea.

00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:49.116
The model is the engine.

00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:50.576
The program around it,

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:51.446
the harness,

00:01:51.456 --> 00:01:52.386
is the car.

00:01:52.396 --> 00:01:55.136
Every approval prompt you've ever clicked came

00:01:55.136 --> 00:01:56.146
from the harness.

00:01:56.236 --> 00:01:58.296
So when an agent does something reckless,

00:01:58.296 --> 00:01:59.936
ask two questions.

00:01:59.936 --> 00:02:01.316
Why did it suggest that?

00:02:01.316 --> 00:02:02.826
And why was it allowed?

00:02:02.836 --> 00:02:04.136
The second one is a setting.

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:05.766
And settings are yours.

00:02:06.605 --> 00:02:08.195
So your job isn't typing.

00:02:08.265 --> 00:02:09.115
It's steering.

00:02:09.265 --> 00:02:10.865
Agents work in a loop.

00:02:10.865 --> 00:02:12.555
Tools set what they can do.

00:02:12.585 --> 00:02:13.525
Check their work,

00:02:13.525 --> 00:02:14.535
and be clear.

00:02:14.545 --> 00:02:16.365
If you've ever managed people,

00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:18.335
you already have the core skill.

00:02:18.405 --> 00:02:19.325
Next up:

00:02:19.325 --> 00:02:20.955
How to Give Good Instructions.
